      "Core Viva Voce: Hardness of Water: What causes temporary hardness? Bicarbonates of calcium and magnesium Ca(HCO_3)_2, Mg(HCO_3)_2; What causes permanent hardness? Chlorides and sulfates of calcium and magnesium CaCl_2, MgSO_4; Why is hardness expressed in terms of CaCO_3? Because CaCO_3 has molecular weight 100 and equivalent weight 50, simplifying mathematical conversions.",
      "Core Viva Voce: EDTA Complexation: Why is disodium salt of EDTA used instead of pure EDTA acid? Free EDTA acid is practically insoluble in water, whereas disodium salt dissolves readily; What is the structure of metal-EDTA complex? Octadentate hexadentate chelate ring where metal ion is encapsulated.",
      "Core Viva Voce: Role of Indicators: Why does EBT change color at endpoint? EBT forms a weak wine-red complex with metal ions; EDTA has higher affinity for Ca^{2+}/Mg^{2+} and snatches metal ions from indicator at endpoint, freeing blue EBT; Why is buffer pH 10 necessary? Below pH 9, metal-EDTA complexes decompose; above pH 11, Mg(OH)_2 precipitates.",
